---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { EMAIL, DIRECCION_EN } from '../../lib/contacto';

// El dominio sale de `site` en astro.config.mjs, su fuente única, igual que
// canonical y sitemap. Aquí no se declara: se lee.
if (!Astro.site) {
  throw new Error('astro.config.mjs debe definir `site`: de ahí sale el dominio publicado en esta página.');
}
const siteOrigin = Astro.site.origin;
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy of Alonso & Campos Advisors S.L. in accordance with the GDPR and the LOPDGDD."
  lang="en"
>

  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--gold)">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="display-title" style="color:var(--white);">Privacy <em style="color:var(--gold);">Policy</em></h1>
      <p style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.65);font-size:1rem;max-width:560px;margin-top:1rem;line-height:1.75;">
        In accordance with Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) and Organic Law 3/2018 (LOPDGDD).
        Last updated: 22 August 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="background:var(--white);">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="policy-body">

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>1. Data controller</h2>
          <table class="policy-table">
            <tbody>
              <tr><th>Legal name</th><td>Alonso &amp; Campos Advisors S.L.</td></tr>
              <tr><th>Tax ID (CIF)</th><td>Pending registration</td></tr>
              <tr><th>Registered address</th><td>{DIRECCION_EN}</td></tr>
              <tr><th>Email</th><td><a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a></td></tr>
              <tr><th>Website</th><td>{siteOrigin}</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>2. Data we collect</h2>
          <p>
            This website has no forms and does not collect data by itself. The only personal data
            we process are those you choose to include in the email you send us: the address you
            write from and whatever you decide to say in the message or attach to it.
          </p>
          <p>We do not collect special categories of personal data, nor do we carry out automated profiling.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>3. Purpose of processing</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Managing and responding to enquiries received by email.</li>
            <li>Assessing the fit between the received enquiry and the firm's services.</li>
            <li>Maintaining the pre-contractual or contractual relationship arising from the initial contact.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>
          {/* PENDIENTE VALIDACIÓN JURÍDICA */}
          <p>
            Where the email comes from a prospective client enquiring about the firm's services,
            the legal basis is the application of <strong>pre-contractual measures</strong>
            requested by the data subject (<strong>Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR</strong>).
          </p>
          <p>
            For all other correspondence received, the legal basis is the controller's
            <strong>legitimate interest</strong> in handling and replying to it
            (<strong>Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR</strong>).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>5. Retention period</h2>
          {/* TODO: plazos pendientes de revisión jurídica. Contrastar los tres/cinco años
               citados con el art. 1964.2 del Código Civil y el art. 30 del Código de Comercio. */}
          <p>
            Data will be retained for as long as necessary to handle the enquiry and, where applicable,
            for the duration of the contractual relationship. Once concluded, data will be kept in a
            blocked state for the applicable statutory limitation periods (generally three years for
            civil claims and five years for commercial obligations).
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>6. Recipients</h2>
          <p>Data are not transferred to third parties except as required by law. The following providers are involved:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub, Inc., USA) — website hosting.</li>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc., USA) — DNS provider for the domain.</li>
            {/* TODO: confirmar la entidad contratante de Google Workspace (Google Ireland Ltd. o Google LLC). */}
            <li><strong>Google Workspace</strong> (Google) — email service where correspondence is received and stored.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Any international transfers that may occur are covered by the standard contractual
            clauses approved by the European Commission.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>7. Data subject rights</h2>
          {/* TODO: acreditación de identidad pendiente de revisión jurídica. La AEPD viene señalando
               que exigir copia del DNI por defecto resulta desproporcionado. */}
          {/* TODO: retirado el consentimiento (6.1.a) como base, revisar si procede mantener
               el apartado "Withdrawal of consent" de esta lista. */}
          <p>You may exercise the following rights against the controller at any time:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Access:</strong> to know what data we process about you.</li>
            <li><strong>Rectification:</strong> to correct inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
            <li><strong>Erasure:</strong> to request deletion of your data when no longer necessary.</li>
            <li><strong>Restriction:</strong> to request that we suspend processing in certain circumstances.</li>
            <li><strong>Portability:</strong> to receive your data in a structured, commonly used format.</li>
            <li><strong>Objection:</strong> to object to processing based on legitimate interest.</li>
            <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent:</strong> at any time, without retroactive effect.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            To exercise your rights, send an email to
            <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>
            indicating the right you wish to exercise and attaching a copy of your identity document.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you consider that the processing does not comply with applicable regulations, you may lodge
            a complaint with the <strong>Spanish Data Protection Agency</strong> (AEPD) at
            <a href="https://www.aepd.es" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">www.aepd.es</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>8. Security</h2>
          <p>
            We implement the technical and organisational measures necessary to ensure the security of
            your data and prevent its alteration, loss, unauthorised processing or access, having regard
            to the state of the art, the nature of the data and the risks to which it is exposed.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>9. Cookies</h2>
          <p>
            This website does not use proprietary tracking or advertising cookies. Browser local storage
            may be used exclusively for the technical operation of the site.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-block">
          <h2>10. Amendments</h2>
          <p>
            We reserve the right to update this policy to adapt it to legislative changes or changes
            to the services provided. The current version will always be available on this page.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="policy-back">
          <a href="/en/contacto/" class="btn btn-outline">← Back to contact</a>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    background: var(--night);
    padding: 5rem 0 4rem;
    background-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 60% 80% at 80% 50%, rgba(61,90,128,0.3) 0%, transparent 70%);
  }

  .policy-body { max-width: 780px; }
  .policy-block { margin-bottom: 3rem; }

  .policy-block h2 {
    font-family: var(--ff-display);
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--night);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--gold);
    display: inline-block;
  }

  .policy-block p { color: var(--text); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; }
  .policy-block ul { margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem 1.25rem; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.8; }
  .policy-block ul li { margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .policy-block a { color: var(--slate); text-decoration: underline; }
  .policy-block a:hover { color: var(--night); }

  .policy-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 0.75rem; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .policy-table th,
  .policy-table td { padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); text-align: left; vertical-align: top; line-height: 1.6; }
  .policy-table th { background: var(--ivory); color: var(--night); font-weight: 600; width: 38%; }
  .policy-table td { color: var(--text); }
  .policy-table td a { color: var(--slate); text-decoration: underline; }

  .policy-back { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
</style>
